Hi Steve.  I can think of two options:

1.  Completely general, allow user to upload a stan program and data and it runs.  The trouble with this is that lots of models will fail or just run too slowly.

2.  Implement one model at a time.  Start with regularized logistic regression using informative priors scaled to the variance of the predictors (for example, b_j ~  t_7(0,1/s_j) priors, where s_j is the sd of x_j in the data).  This should be stable and fast (to be really fast it could just use stan-optimize).

Option 1 would be our dream.  It could make sense to start with option 2 to get foot in the door.  But I don’t really know, I think that Bob and others on stan-dev might have clearer thoughts.
A

