On Sunday, February 21, 2016, Steve Scott <steve...@google.com> wrote:
>
> Now back to the ui.  The original winbugs had an interface where people could draw the dag for their model using nodes and arrows.  Is that something that would be worth pursuing with Stan?

It's much less straightforward to do something like that for Stan compared to winbugs, which is a graphical modeling language. Stan's language allows for models impossible to program in winbugs, but going from dag to Stan model is tricky. That said, a graphical modeling wrapper for Stan is definitely something we've discussed, but it's not an easy project. It would be great though.

Jonah

