I actually don’t think it would be so hard to set up something that would translate Bugs-style graphical models to Stan.  That would allow a subset of Stan models to be fit.  To me I don’t see this as easier than just writing the Stan model directly.  I guess different things are easier for different users.  Again, one option could be to start with some particular models such as regularized logistic regression and nonparametric curve fitting.  But in any case I recognize the learning curve of Stan, that’s one reason I like the idea of having it on the web, so users can experiment with it without having to download the software onto their own computers.
A

