Hi Robert,

I think there's a little confusion and hopefully we can sort it out.

William Buchanan's pull request was on github.com/stan-dev/statastan's <http://github.com/stan-dev/statastan's> gh-pages branch. (gh-pages is the branch, not master) By creating the gh-pages branch on stan-dev/statastan and merging his branch into that branch allowed for serving a project page:
https://stan-dev.github.io/statastan
(this should redirect to https://mc-stan.org/statastan)

The updates to that particular branch hasn't really changed any of the http://mc-stan.org behavior. (You can access http://mc-stan.org/statastan by typing that directly, but it's not linked from anything on mc-stan.org <http://mc-stan.org>.)

To update mc-stan.org <http://mc-stan.org>, you want to checkout this repository, update it, and create a pull request against the master branch:
https://github.com/stan-dev/stan-dev.github.io

That's the repo for our website. For concreteness, interfaces/stata-stan.md <http://stata-stan.md>
(see: https://github.com/stan-dev/stan-dev.github.io/blob/master/interfaces/stata-stan.md)
gets rendered into this page:
http://mc-stan.org/interfaces/stata-stan.html

So... what are you trying to do? Did you want to provide the content on the stan-dev/statastan's gh-pages branch directly at http://mc-stan.org/interfaces/stata-stan.html? Alternatively, did you want a link to the project page from mc-stan.org/interfaces/stata-stan.html <http://mc-stan.org/interfaces/stata-stan.html>?

Daniel

